// Ecat_8_5_424                Christof, thou must do my bidding. Should’st thou flee our Haven, our enemies would rend thee asunder for the pleasure of seeing thy Brujah blood run in rivulets down the paving stones.
// Christof_8_5_425            And why should I not die? I crave the solace of the sepulcher; the peace that only clamorous death may bring.
// Ecat_8_5_426                Has not thy Lord forbidden it?
// Christof_8_5_427            Alas, thou speaks true. The Almighty commands that I not perish by mine own hand. And yet, have I not perished already? Can the dead die again?
// Ecat_8_5_428                How simple is thy creed. Does it stand when tested by the complexity of the world? Thy laws apply only to thy life and thy death. Not thy unlife.
// Christof_8_5_429            I live on, yet I am not alive. I have died, yet I am not dead. Though I have perished, my soul is neither in heaven nor hell, though hell this seems.
// Ecat_8_5_430                And so thou must continue to follow the law 'gainst self-slaughter, even in un-death.
